{
  "_comment": "Free metric-compatible substitutes for common commercial source fonts. Keys are matched (case-insensitive, substring) against the PostScript / source font name extracted from the PDF. The first matching rule wins, so list more specific rules first. `family` must exist in python/pdf-editor FONT_FILE_VARIANTS. `weight` is one of light/normal/bold; `style` is normal/italic. Used by python/pdf-editor/apply_annotations_direct_new.py:resolve_substitute_font_entry when the runtime-extracted subset can't cover the requested text.",
